          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">9. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Who makes Centr treadmills?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Centr, the fitness brand founded by Chris Hemsworth, makes them with Inspire Fitness, a Southern California equipment maker. HighPost Capital acquired both companies in 2022 and combined them, which is why Costco lists Centr equipment as "Centr by Inspire Fitness". Centr’s store also sells Inspire Series treadmills.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How much is the Centr x HYROX Perform Tread?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Centr and Perform Better both listed it at $6,999 on 5 November 2026. A Costco listing in search results showed $5,999, which we could not confirm on the day. Prices change, so check before buying.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What are the Centr x HYROX Perform Tread specs?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Centr and Perform Better agree on a motorless curved slat deck, a 59 by 19-inch running area, eight magnetic resistance levels, a 396.8 lb (180 kg) maximum user, a 400 lb assembled weight and a 74 by 42.5-inch footprint. Its height is listed as 67.3 inches by Centr and 59.2 inches by Perform Better.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the Centr Runr folding tool-less assembly treadmill?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                It is Costco’s listing name for the Centr Runr, Centr’s folding motorized treadmill without a screen. Centr lists a 3.0 HP brushless motor, 1 to 10 mph, a 20 by 55-inch running surface, a 300 lb maximum user and tool-free setup, with a lifetime frame and motor warranty. Centr sold it for $1,299 on 5 November 2026.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the difference between the Centr Runr and Runr-S?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                The Runr-S adds a 10-inch touchscreen with streaming apps, Bluetooth speakers, smartphone mirroring and 25 programs. The motor, deck, speed, 300 lb rating, footprint and warranty are the same. On 5 November 2026 Centr listed the Runr at $1,299 and the Runr-S at $1,699.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is the Centr Runr good for running?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                It suits walking and jogging better than running. Its 55-inch deck is short for taller runners at speed, the top speed is 10 mph and the rating is 300 lb, all below many treadmills at its price. Its strength is a lifetime warranty on the frame and motor.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is the HYROX treadmill worth it for home use?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                For a serious HYROX competitor who wants the race machine, it can be. For general curved-treadmill running, the TrueForm Trainer or AssaultRunner Pro cost about half as much, and the Tru Grit Runner offers sled-push settings for about a third of the price.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buying a Centr Treadmill</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Centr’s brand is strong and its treadmill range is narrow, which leads to a few predictable mismatches.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying the Runr for serious running</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">A 55-inch deck and a 10 mph top speed suit walking and jogging. Taller runners and anyone doing fast intervals should look at a treadmill with a 60-inch deck, including the Inspire T5 on Centr’s own store.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Paying for the screen you will not use</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The Runr-S costs $400 more than the Runr for a 10-inch touchscreen. If you already watch a tablet or TV while you walk, the Runr does everything else the Runr-S does.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying the Perform Tread as an everyday treadmill</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">A motorless curved treadmill is hard work at any speed. It is superb for HYROX intervals and sled work, and tiring for long easy runs. If you want both, you may need a motorized treadmill as well, which changes the budget.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Measuring for the wrong height</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Sellers list the Perform Tread’s height at 59.2, 65 or 67.3 inches. For a basement with a low ceiling or a tight doorway, plan for the tallest figure and ask the seller for shipping dimensions before ordering a 400 lb machine.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

