        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Centr sells three treadmills: the folding Runr ($1,299) and Runr-S ($1,699),
          and the motorless Centr x HYROX Perform Tread ($6,999), the official HYROX race treadmill.</strong> The
          Runr models are walking and jogging treadmills with a better-than-usual lifetime frame and motor
          warranty but a short 55-inch deck and a 10 mph top speed.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The Perform Tread is a strong curved treadmill with real resistance and a sled-push mode, and worth its
          price mainly to HYROX athletes. Everyone else should compare the
          <a href="/trueform-treadmills/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">TrueForm Trainer</a> and
          the <a href="/best-curved-treadmills/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">other curved treadmills</a>
          at about half the money.
          </p>
